Well, now we're starting to get more down to earth.  I can see that
an extension of the 'exit' semantics of a MUD to refer to a location
on a different city could be accomplished, which is virtually the
same structural model used in the World-Wide-Web, which explains
their reliance on Mosiac as an interface paradigm (and WWW-based
services are themselves growing like weeds, so that's a hot area).
Ditto for object transfer, though there are nightmarish problems
even in these modest facilities (e.g. consistency guarantees, distributed
transaction protocols, and nameservers).  Similarly, I suppose that
gatways to existing internet services aren't particularly challenging.

